comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-30T10:27:25.583Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: health --check-only now defaults to summary verdict output with empty passing evidence bodies; --full retains complete diagnostics and explicit brief/summary preserve fast optional-scan behavior."
  "2026-07-30T11:24:16.147Z","harness:codex","Delivery boundary: --check-only now returns the summary verdict by default while still running every check, and --full restores evidence. The canonical issue remains open until health is added to the representative token-budget corpus with measured before/after evidence and agent-guidance coverage."
  "2026-07-30T11:30:57.231Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/829 reviews cohesive SDK context budgets, universal row contracts, bounded graph/health diagnostics, quality ratchets, and exact-head commit e53544cd1."
  "2026-07-30T17:15:06.358Z","harness:claude-code","Verified shipped 2026-07-30 (evening) at HEAD. health --check-only is now verdict-first and the reduction is 115-fold: 1,503 bytes against 172,990 bytes for the plain form, with the complete evidence still reachable through the escape hatch at 172,991 bytes. The summary form is now byte-identical to check-only at 1,503, so the two spellings agree rather than differing by one byte as they did when this was filed. The extensions activation sub-object that was 47 percent of the whole payload is no longer emitted on the verdict path.\n\nRecording as evidence rather than closing. Two things this item raised are worth confirming before it closes. The repository guidance that routes agents to check-only is now correct advice, so the documentation half is satisfied by the code rather than needing a doc change. And the surviving question is discoverability: check-only, summary, brief and full are four spellings on one command with three of them now producing the same output, which is the bounding-vocabulary problem tracked on the simplification initiative rather than a diagnostics defect. Linked the shipped contract spec to this item with its runnable command so the proof is reachable from the tracker."
  "2026-09-06T10:40:16.410Z","harness:codex","Verification: the existing token-budget gate passes all 32 surfaces, including the health default ceiling, unbounded negative control, and infeasible-intent receipt. The new compact health verdict retains the existing budget without raising thresholds. Full typecheck passes; final coverage and static pipelines are still running."
  "2026-09-06T10:58:48.289Z","harness:codex","The authored assurance derive, risk, and lineages intents improve discovery while reducing the existing complete-task transcript composite from its 12667-token ceiling to 12658 tokens. The contracts-plus-next orientation is 4820 tokens against the unchanged 4829 ceiling. All 8 tasks and 21 steps complete; no token thresholds were raised."
  "2026-09-06T11:21:55.114Z","harness:codex","Final live diagnostic measurement on the 2650-item tracker: JSON check-only 3635 bytes versus full evidence 90770 bytes (24.97x smaller). Both returned ok true, the same ten per-check booleans/statuses, and verdict authority ok with exit_code 0; integrity remains advisory warn. The original report measured 132585 bytes for the formerly inert check-only flag. Current token-budget gate passes all 32 surfaces, its unbounded negative control and infeasible-intent receipt, without raising ceilings. Source/static correctness gates passed through tracker assurance; import-time timing gates will be repeated after full coverage releases CPU."
  "2026-09-06T11:26:05.543Z","harness:codex","Delivery verification: full suite passes all 8495 tests in 627 files at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. The guidance integration test checks the actual AGENTS.md recommended command, verifies a passing check omits evidence, and restores full detail explicitly. The health-default token ceiling and complete-task token gates pass unchanged. Packed consumers and Bun SDK/CLI execution pass; final hosted review and release evidence follow independently."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-30T09:21:19.724Z","harness:claude-code","Re-measured 2026-07-30 at HEAD, after PR 818 shipped bounded projections and snapshot lease safety. The bounded-projection wave did not reach this command. pm health plain = 127,582 B; pm health --check-only = 127,583 B (one byte MORE than plain); pm health --summary = 727 B. The cheap form is 175x smaller than the form AGENTS.md routes agents to under When Unsure, and --check-only remains exactly as inert as when this item was filed. A new bounded-projection primitive existing in the SDK while this consumer cannot reach it is the seam pattern, not a fix."
